  "id": "DrugBank_DB01262 - MONDO_15667",
  "verbalization": "Decitabine is associated with Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia through a chain of indications that link it to Mitoxantrone and Daunorubicin, both of which are known to be used in the treatment of Acute Myeloid Leukemia. The evidence suggests that Decitabine may be repurposed for this condition, as it shares a common pathway with other drugs used in the management of similar leukemias. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, each linking Decitabine to a different drug that ultimately targets Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia, supports the hypothesis that Decitabine could be a potential therapeutic option for this condition. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Mitoxantrone and Daunorubicin in the treatment of this leukemia type, and the possibility that Decitabine may function similarly in the context of Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia.",
